course: dictionary
lesson: 12033
title: Splitting colours with chromatography
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Chromatography is a way to separate a mixture into the different substances inside it. Some colours look like one colour, but they are really made of several hidden colours.
explain: «Mia put a black dot of ink on filter paper and dipped the edge in water.» As the water moved up the paper, it carried the colours with it. Each colour travelled at its own speed, so they spread apart and showed up as separate bands.
explain: Scientists use the same idea to test food, medicines and crime evidence. The paper or picture that shows the separated colours is called a «chromatogram».
fact: Chromatography means separating a mixture into the different substances in it.
fact: «Chromatography» is an uncountable noun, so you say chromatography, not chromatographies.
fact: «Chromatogram» is the result: the picture made by chromatography.
fact: In paper chromatography, each substance moves at its own speed, so the colours end up in different places on the paper.
exercise: «Mia split her black ink with chromatography.» What is chromatography? | A way of mixing paints together | A type of paper that never gets wet | *A way of separating a mixture into the substances in it | A kind of camera for taking photos
exercise: In the paper experiment, why do the colours end up in different places? | They are all stuck in one spot | *They move at different speeds | They are different sizes of paper | They are painted on in different colours
exercise: The word «chromatogram» names what? | The water used in the test | The scientist who runs the test | *The picture made by chromatography | The filter paper cut into a circle
test: Which of these is a place where scientists use chromatography? | Toy shops | Football pitches | *Food testing labs | Bus stations
test: What do you need to start a simple paper chromatography test? | A pencil and a ruler | A cup of tea and a spoon | A sheet of glass and a torch | *A felt-tip dot on filter paper, and water
exam: What does chromatography do to a mixture of colours? | Makes the colours brighter | Blends the colours into one new colour | Hides the colours inside a cup | *Splits it into its separate colours
